## Summary

Compress the controlled programming-agent section from a condition list, question list, and repeated qualifications into two paragraphs.

The shorter version retains only the boundaries needed by the program article:

- theory conditions and matched starting components;
- treatment-induced machinery changes as outcomes;
- delayed demands that expose earlier mistakes;
- causal revision and coherent modification at comparable cost;
- the additional later-production requirement for a factory-learning claim;
- conclusions limited to the contrasts actually run.

Detailed protocol design remains outside the article. This PR changes one section in one file and leaves the merged Naurian argument untouched.
